From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius DKM <mariusdkm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:54:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a "metadata" mDNS backend for apps with their own
 responder

An application that runs Shairport Sync instances and already has an mDNS responder
can publish the services itself, with no Avahi or D-Bus. The backend sends an 'ssnc'
'svrg' item for each service when it is registered and whenever its TXT records
change, and is only used when selected with mdns_backend = "metadata".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ADVANCED TOPICS/RunningMultipleInstances.md |   5 +
 METADATA CODES.md                           |   1 +
 Makefile.am                                 |   2 +-
 mdns.c                                      |   6 +
 mdns_metadata.c                             | 120 ++++++++++++++++++++
 scripts/shairport-sync.conf                 |   2 +-
 6 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 mdns_metadata.c

diff --git a/ADVANCED TOPICS/RunningMultipleInstances.md b/ADVANCED TOPICS/RunningMultipleInstances.md
index 409b6eb..6209137 100644
--- a/ADVANCED TOPICS/RunningMultipleInstances.md
+++ b/ADVANCED TOPICS/RunningMultipleInstances.md
@@ -146,3 +146,8 @@ instance's service under one hostname; instances differ by their service name. I
 would otherwise advertise on interfaces you don't want (internal/container bridges,
 for example), scope it to your LAN interface (`allow-interfaces=` in
 `avahi-daemon.conf`) to keep discovery clean.
+
+An application that runs the instances and has its own mDNS responder can skip
+Avahi: with `mdns_backend = "metadata";` each instance sends its services to the
+metadata feed (`svrg`, see [METADATA CODES](../METADATA%20CODES.md)) and the
+application publishes them while the instance runs.
diff --git a/METADATA CODES.md b/METADATA CODES.md
index c69d6d1..9c62d16 100644
--- a/METADATA CODES.md
+++ b/METADATA CODES.md
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ Shairport SyNC itself).
 | `styp` | Stream type description (e.g. `"Classic"`, `"Realtime"`, `"Buffered"`). |
 | `svip` | The IP address used by the player for the play session. |
 | `svna` | The service name of the player. |
+| `svrg` | `mdns_backend = "metadata"`: register a service, or replace its TXT records. Lines `service=`, `name=`, `port=`, then `txt=<key=value>` per TXT record. Read the feed (e.g. open the metadata pipe) before starting Shairport Sync. |

